<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.9.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01012</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.9.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9be46ff2-f497-4ef2-ba4c-fd0b9c70d320</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
        <exercise id="fb4582f9-6add-436e-a74f-586af09e3a74" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">The graphs show the distance, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, traveled by two cars, A and B, over time, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. Distance is measured in miles, and time is measured in hours. Which car traveled slower? 
          (<media alt="Lines A and B on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_01.svg"/></media>)</para>
            <para id="para-00003">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00004">Car A</para>
            <para id="para-00005">Car B</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00006">Correct! Car A traveled slower because Car B was a farther distance in the same amount of time as Car A.</para>
            <para id="para-00007">Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00008">The correct answer is Car A traveled slower because Car B was a farther distance in the same amount of time as Car A.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_43d7eb08-a3ef-4608-a848-3f943fd46fcc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00009">For questions 2 – 5, use the graphs below to match each description of a situation in which the volume of water in a tank is a function of time to its corresponding graph.</para>
         
                <para id="para-00010">Graph 1
            (<media alt="Graph on coordinate plane, no grid, Origin O. V shaped graph, line begins on Y axis, Vertex points down."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_02.svg"/></media>)</para>
              
                <para id="para-00011">Graph 2
            (<media alt="Graph on coordinate plane, no grid, Origin O. Line begins at origin, moves upwards and to right. Steeper second segment."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_03.svg"/></media>)</para>
              
         
                <para id="para-00012">Graph 3
            (<media alt="Graph on coordinate plane, no grid, Origin O. V shaped graph, line begins on at origin, Vertex points up."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_04.svg"/></media>)</para>
              
                <para id="para-00013">Graph 4
            (<media alt="Graph on coordinate plane, no grid, Origin O. Line begins at origin, moves upwards and to right, decreases briefly, then increases again."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_05.svg"/></media>)</para>
              
            
            <para id="para-00014">An empty 20-gallon water tank is filled at a constant rate for 3 minutes until it is half full. Then, it is emptied at a constant rate for 3 minutes.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00015">Correct! Graph 3</para>
            <para id="para-00016">Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">The correct answer is Graph 3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_04a914d5-1a20-4a61-8d16-2929c8a4328f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00018">A full 10-gallon water tank is drained for 30 seconds, until it is half full. Afterward, it gets refilled.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00019">Correct! Graph 1</para>
            <para id="para-00020">Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">The correct answer is Graph 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1fb4f2f9-3fd6-4178-9685-d6fece3b0815" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00022">A 2,000-gallon water tank starts out empty. It is being filled for 5 hours, slowly at first, and faster later.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00023">Correct! Graph 2</para>
            <para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00025">The correct answer is Graph 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_594de829-a3ec-448e-8b1c-b95c36a43989" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00026">An empty 100-gallon water tank is filled in 50 minutes. Then, a dog jumps in and splashes around for 10 minutes, letting 7 gallons of water out. The tank is refilled afterward.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00027">Correct! Graph 4</para>
            <para id="para-00028">Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00029">The correct answer is Graph 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <para id="para-00030">For questions 6 – 7, use this situation and function:</para>
      <para id="para-00031">
        <quote id="quote-00001">The daily cost to the manufacturing company is modeled by the function \(C(x)=7.25x+2500\), where \(C(x)\) is the total daily cost and \(x\) is the number of items manufactured.</quote>
    </para>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00003">
        <exercise id="f14d1917-2b7c-42b3-9389-2b0ff44689fc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00032">What value equals <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00033">Correct! 2500</para>
            <para id="para-00034">Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00035">The correct answer is 2,500.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fa3eeebd-3640-4077-bc4e-fd233737d66e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00036">What does <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> mean in the context of the situation?</para>
            <para id="para-00037">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00038">When the cost is 0</para>
            <para id="para-00039">Horizontal intercept</para>
            <para id="para-00040">Cost before any items are manufactured</para>
            <para id="para-00041">Maximum cost</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00042">Correct! Cost before any items are manufactured</para>
            <para id="para-00043">Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00044">The correct answer is cost before any items are manufactured.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Do not edit below this line-->
    </section>
  </content>
